<title>ITALY: Bank of Italy buying back up to 2.5 trln lire BOTs.</title>
<headline>Bank of Italy buying back up to 2.5 trln lire BOTs.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Italy said it would buy back up to 2.5 trillion lire of short term bills (BOT) expiring between November 29, 1996 and May 30, 1997.</p>
<p>Bids must be received by 0845 GMT today.</p>
</text>
